  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The justice sector in Mozambique agree /approve a SOP for the Palaces of Justice.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Palaces of Justice at decentralized level facing serious challenges in working as a one stop shop</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Complete the regulatory framework on alternatives to prison. Elaborate the Regulation on the 2019 Code of Execution of Sentences in partnership with SERNAP.
- Strengthen the human resources capacity of the Mozambique legal aid system through supporting the qualification of 30 trainees as public defenders in partnership with CFJJ/IPAJ.
- Complete the curriculum revision of the CFJJ in the area of Alternatives to Prison, HR, HIV/AIDS and GBV and trained at least 15 trainees of the CFJJ
- Complete Baseline Study on Access to Justice</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Completed the initial 6 month training of 30 public defenders of the IPAJ with the CFJJ
- Completed the Manual for Justice Professionals on Alternatives to Prison and the Manual on Human Rights, GBV, HIV/AIDS and trained a total of 55 officials (23 M and 22 W) from the Judiciary, the Attorney General, Academia Teachers, Police Academies and CSOs 
- Baseline Study almost finalized (preliminary report submitted)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In synergy with 00126266

- Finalize the process of consultation of the law on community courts
- Close project and ensure transition to new project cycle</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Draft Law finalized
- Project closed and transitional activities conducted
- Project evaluation finalized</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Train magistrates, prosecutors, public defenders and other law judicial actors on Alternatives to Prison, HR, GBV, HIV/AIDS
- Finalize two knowledge products for further advocacy and evidence based lobby on justice reform, namely, Baseline Study on A2J and Needs Assessment of Legal Aid in Mozambique
- Roll-out the Pilot Mobile court and conduct at least one pilot regional campaign</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Trained, through the mandatory initial training provided by the CFJJ to magistrates, prosecutors and legal aid providers, 100 future justice professionals on A2P, HR, GBV, HIV/AIDS
- Publicly launched the IPAJ needs assessment and conducted lobby and advocacy at the executive level for justice reform. Finalized the BL study on A2J
- Piloted itinerant justice campaign in Maputo Province through mobile court, in remote areas, benefitting 29 declarants, 11 M and 18 W (8 youth), 16 inmates of which 13 in pre-trial detention, totally completing 13 court cases in Maputo Provincial Courts Jurisdiction.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
